    "physical_note": "Yukawa length = 10.0 kpc vs galaxy r_max = 30 kpc. m0*r_max = 3.0 >> 1 means field decays exponentially across galaxy. Flat rotation curves need rho ~ 1/r^2; Yukawa gives rho ~ exp(-2m0*r)/r^2. V=(lambda/4)Psi^4 is too local (proportional to Psi^3, subdominant at small Psi) to reshape the profile from exponential to power-law."
